<title>AUSTRIA: IRAN SAYS OPEC SUCCESS DEPENDS ON QUOTA ADHERENCE.</title>
<headline>IRAN SAYS OPEC SUCCESS DEPENDS ON QUOTA ADHERENCE.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian oil minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh said the success of OPEC's meeting this week depended on convincing those members who are violating quotas to adhere to official allocations.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything depends on the violations. Any decision without stopping the violations does not pay,&quot; he told reporters.  </p>
<p>He reiterated that OPEC was overproducing.</p>
<p>The producer group's current ceiling is 25.033 million barrels per day (bpd) but actual output is running around 2.0 million bpd above that.</p>
<p>Aghazadeh is to chair OPEC's three-man quota compliance committee meeting scheduled for 1300 GMT today. The other members are the oil ministers of Indonesia and Nigeria.</p>
<p>The full OPEC conference is set to start on Wednesday afternoon local time.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
